%% Non-streaming request round trip. The provider only ever sees the
%% placeholder; the client receives the restored real value. Optional Open WebUI
%% is a backend HTTP client, with a separate browser/Caddy hop and raw history.
%% Render: scripts/render_diagrams.sh (PNG committed next to this source).
%% animate: the request/response flow moves; scripts/animate_diagrams.py renders the
%% animated SVG + GIF committed next to this source (a '%% animate' marker opts in).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant T as Tool / WebUI backend
    participant P as llm-redact proxy
    participant W as NER worker thread
    participant V as Vault (local)
    participant L as LLM provider

    Note left of T: Optional WebUI: browser → Caddy → backend<br/>raw prompts and restored replies stay in history
    T->>P: POST recognized chat route<br/>"…email jane@corp.example…"
    activate P
    P->>P: collect the strings the redaction<br/>will scan (every JSON string value)
    P->>W: [detection.ner] only: NER on a worker<br/>thread — off the event loop
    W-->>P: each string's model detections
    P->>P: detect + resolve overlaps, taking the<br/>precomputed NER results (synchronous)
    P->>V: token for (session, EMAIL, value)<br/>— one vault transaction per request
    V-->>P: «EMAIL_001» — deterministic:<br/>same value ⇒ same token
    P->>L: "…email «EMAIL_001»…"<br/>(+ system note: reproduce tokens exactly)
    deactivate P
    L-->>P: 200 "Sure, I drafted the email to «EMAIL_001»"
    activate P
    P->>V: reverse lookup «EMAIL_001»
    V-->>P: jane@corp.example
    P-->>T: "Sure, I drafted the email to jane@corp.example"
    deactivate P
    Note over T,L: Tools may use /v1/messages, WebUI uses /v1/chat/completions.<br/>Client-key auth passes through, oversized redactable bodies → 413.
